Theorem VF-2: Layer 2 AIMS contract consistency and neutral fact validation

  Preconditions:
    - VF-2 governs the Layer-2 contract-consistency verifier per Annex E §AIMS VF-2: "independent contract-consistency (NOT a filter over VF-1)."
      Four checks: (a) parameters declared Absent MUST have no live uses;
      (b) RL-31 neutral parameter-disjointness facts backed by a disjointness
      proof; (c) RL-29 FreshSelfAllocationFacts match IC-4
      returns_fresh_self_alloc; (d) RL-30 MemoryAccessFact is derivable from
      IC-5, parameter contracts, and realized operations.
    - The ARC verifier owns (a). The executable realization boundary validates
      exact coverage and contract agreement for the conservative (b)/(c)/(d)
      fact carriers. Complete RL-31 provenance precision remains target-only.
      Target attribute or metadata spelling is outside VF-2 and is checked by
      backend projection fidelity.
    - VF-2 carries the common signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap x
      MemoryContract -> Result () (List VerifyError) per
      aims-proof/proofs/01-verification/Verification.proof. Discharged here
      against the sec-01 Verification.proof sorry obligation.
    - Shipped verifier site:
        * compiler/ori_arc/src/verify/mod.rs
          check_function_with_contract reports VerifyError::AbsentParamHasUses
          (the only Layer-2 variant currently emitted; it is NOT a whole-lattice
          oracle — that is VF-3).
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-2 (Absent) soundness is load-bearing for the
      AbsentParamHasUses check.
    - depends-on sec-06: IC-3 ParamContract + IC-5 EffectSummary soundness is
      load-bearing for the neutral (b)/(c)/(d) checks.
    - depends-on sec-08: the neutral (b)/(c)/(d) checks are conditional on
      RL-31 (b), RL-29 (c), RL-30 (d) discharging in sec-08; (b)'s cross-call-site
      provenance also exercises the interprocedural_summary engine.

  Soundness property:
    Forall realized ArcFunction F with inferred MemoryContract C:

      (P1) Implemented-check soundness: AbsentParamHasUses fires for parameter
           p of F IFF p is declared Cardinality = Absent in C AND p has a live
           use on some forward-reachable path of F. (The contract claimed the
           parameter is never used; the IR uses it — a contract-vs-realization
           inconsistency.) A non-Absent parameter, or an Absent parameter with
           no live use, is consistent.

      (P2) Conditional soundness of (b)/(c)/(d): each neutral fact check is
           sound ASSUMING its sec-08 backend-neutral derivation rule discharged —
           (b) sound given RL-31 (disjointness proof), (c) sound given RL-29
           (returns_fresh_self_alloc), (d) sound given RL-30 (IC-5 +
           ParamContract + realized-operation derivation). Freezing any of
           (b)/(c)/(d) WITHOUT the underlying sec-08 proof would assert
           unproven facts, so each is gated on its dependency.

    VF-2 is an INDEPENDENT layer, not a filter over VF-1: a structurally
    well-formed function (VF-1 clean) can still carry a contract inconsistency
    (VF-2 dirty), and vice versa. The two layers catch disjoint failure classes.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the structural_induction engine via
    contract-consistency soundness (per the proof-checker design
    sec-Engine-per-Category-Inventory VF row; the foundational-axiom policy
    sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape).

    Part (P1) — AbsentParamHasUses decision grid:

      The verifier enumerates a (param_absent, has_live_forward_use) grid and
      asserts the check fires exactly on (Absent AND has-use):
        (Absent, has-use) -> error (contract violated)
        (Absent, no-use) -> no error (consistent)
        (non-Absent, has-use) -> no error (consistent — uses permitted)
        (non-Absent, no-use) -> no error (consistent)
      Coverage gate: 4 decisions.

    Part (P2) — neutral-fact conditional soundness:

      The verifier confirms the conditional implication for each of (b)/(c)/(d):
      (the sec-08 rule discharged) implies (the check is sound). RL-31 / RL-29 /
      RL-30 are each discharged in sec-08, so (b)/(c)/(d) are each conditionally
      sound. Coverage gate: 3 neutral-fact checks; richer RL-31 provenance and
      RL-30 region precision remain target work.

    Negative-direction witness:
      A neutral fact check is NOT sound when its sec-08 dependency is
      UNDISCHARGED — freezing (b)/(c)/(d) without the underlying RL proof would
      assert unproven facts. The verifier confirms the undischarged case is
      rejected.

    Engines dispatched:
      structural_induction (PRIMARY — section_09::verify_vf2_contract_consistency;
        AbsentParamHasUses decision grid + (b)/(c)/(d) conditional soundness;
        emits Fail on a decision mismatch or a wrongly-accepted undischarged
        neutral fact check)
      interprocedural_summary (CO-DISPATCH for (b) cross-call-site provenance —
        gracious-accept at the SECONDARY position once structural_induction has
        discharged)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_09 structural_induction engine discharges VF-2 via (P1) the AbsentParamHasUses decision grid (fires iff an Absent parameter has a live forward-reachable use, over 4 decisions) and (P2) conditional soundness of the neutral (b) RL-31 / (c) RL-29 / (d) RL-30 fact checks (each sound exactly when its sec-08 backend-neutral derivation rule is discharged, with a negative witness rejecting the undischarged case), with target spelling fidelity intentionally excluded
